-- title:
--   Local containment preserves the supplement property
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a profinite group, let $N\trianglelefteq G$ be closed, and let $H,J\le G$ be closed. Suppose $NJ=G$. If for every prime $p$ some Sylow pro-$p$ subgroup of $J$ has a $G$-conjugate contained in $H$, then
--
--   $$NH=G.$$
--
--   This transfers the supplement property along local containment and supplies a structural input for local conjugacy and fixed-point arguments.
-- source:
--   Michael C. Burkhart, Local conjugacy in prosolvable groups, https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.37678; supporting formalization lemma, LocalConjugacy/LocalSupplement.lean, lines 49–73; source SHA-256 f1034a8ac923c57c992bf6e1e92c87e4819827b792e33ad753c4d18508d1c398.

